1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,910
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,010 --> 00:00:03,480
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,040
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:09,210
The men Ms. Yang showed us today
were all pretty good, weren't they?

5
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:13,590
I thought that mechanical
engineering professor...

6
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:16,490
would look especially good
with Director Joo.

7
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:20,260
I mean, one past divorce...

8
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:22,990
isn't a big deal
given Director Joo's age,

9
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:24,660
and he has no kids.

10
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:26,030
With that kind of background,

11
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,800
I think he'd be perfect for her.

12
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:31,840
Your problem is that
you're a total busybody.

13
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:35,640
What, a busybody?

14
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:37,910
Did Director Joo ask you
to set her up with a man?

15
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:39,510
She didn't.

16
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:42,350
Does she really have to
say it out loud?

17
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:44,250
Bosses are supposed
to take the hint...

18
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:46,120
and handle these things for them.

19
00:00:46,350 --> 00:00:47,890
This is all out of affection,
you know.

20
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:49,590
Planning something like this...

21
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:52,360
without considering her feelings
isn't caring,

22
00:00:52,360 --> 00:00:53,360
it's hypocritical.

23
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:57,360
Come on, why do you have to
look at it like that?

24
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:59,260
Director Joo should meet
a good man...

25
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:00,800
and know what it feels like
to be loved.

26
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,230
Right, and I'm saying
you don't need...

27
00:01:03,570 --> 00:01:06,040
to go out of your way
to find that nice man.

28
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:08,110
Honey.

29
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:11,210
Didn't you see
how flustered she was earlier?

30
00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:14,580
How can a boss be so clueless?

31
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:48,350
Even if the fish is in the net,

32
00:01:49,550 --> 00:01:51,380
you still have to poke it
once in a while...

33
00:01:52,050 --> 00:01:54,020
to make sure it stays alive.

34
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,860
Yes, just like today,

35
00:01:59,220 --> 00:02:01,460
every time Kim Jung Sun
stirs things up,

36
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:03,700
it works out in my favor.

37
00:02:14,940 --> 00:02:18,610
No. No woman ever lived here.

38
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:22,650
Only an old man lived here
all his life,

39
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:26,550
and he passed away last year.

40
00:02:28,720 --> 00:02:31,790
But Dad said Director Joo
gave him this address.

41
00:02:35,190 --> 00:02:38,430
Was Director Joo behind all of this
from the very start?

42
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
I see.

43
00:02:41,470 --> 00:02:44,170
If Director Joo
ever approaches you first,

44
00:02:44,670 --> 00:02:47,110
please pass along whatever she says
to me. Okay?

45
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:55,080
Did Attorney Seo know?

46
00:02:56,710 --> 00:02:59,250
That Director Joo could be
my birth mother?

47
00:03:07,430 --> 00:03:10,630
Why on earth is that woman
paying us money...

48
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:12,400
just to kick us out?

49
00:03:13,570 --> 00:03:14,830
Isn't it obvious?

50
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,500
She said it's because of Eun Guk.

51
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:18,940
What about him?

52
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:21,940
He's got good looks, a great build,

53
00:03:22,010 --> 00:03:24,080
and an amazing personality.

54
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:26,910
Plus,
he's never been married before.

55
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:31,720
A man like our Eun Guk
is way out of her league.

56
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,650
Well, that's just what you think.

57
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:35,320
You're a woman yourself,

58
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:36,750
so how can you not understand
other women?

59
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,560
Because of how he is,

60
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:43,700
that might just make her feel
more uncomfortable.

61
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,060
What do you know?

62
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,600
It takes a woman to know a woman.

63
00:03:48,370 --> 00:03:49,870
It's not discomfort at all.

64
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:54,210
She's totally smitten
every single time she sees him.

65
00:03:54,870 --> 00:03:58,040
Come on, do you honestly think
all women think like you?

66
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:01,210
Whatever.

67
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:05,350
Should we take this money
and move somewhere nice,

68
00:04:05,920 --> 00:04:09,250
or try to borrow more...

69
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:12,020
to get a yearly lease apartment?

70
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:14,060
Mom,

71
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:15,960
Teun Teun's mom...

72
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,960
just lost her only sibling
a couple of days ago.

73
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:21,270
Do you want to bleed
someone like that dry?

74
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,730
Have some conscience.

75
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:26,140
Those are
two completely separate things.

76
00:04:26,970 --> 00:04:29,110
Anyway, this is an absolute no.

77
00:04:29,810 --> 00:04:31,410
I clearly told you no.

78
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:35,180
You're so stubborn. Fine, you brat.

79
00:04:37,150 --> 00:04:38,620
Unbelievable.

80
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:46,220
What are you doing?

81
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,630
I'm closing the cafe for a while.

82
00:04:49,630 --> 00:04:51,200
You should take
a little more time off.

83
00:04:51,730 --> 00:04:53,060
I'll cover the cafe for you.

84
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:56,830
No. From today on,
stay out of my cafe's business.

85
00:04:57,240 --> 00:04:58,240
Boss.

86
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:05,080
Do you really think
you'll be okay if I leave?

87
00:05:07,710 --> 00:05:10,450
Will it really give you
peace of mind if I leave?

88
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:11,920
Yes.

89
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:14,050
At least I'll feel lighter
than I do right now.

90
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:16,250
Fine.

91
00:05:16,950 --> 00:05:17,960
I'll go.

92
00:05:19,190 --> 00:05:20,190
Still,

93
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:22,790
even if I do leave,
it won't be right away.

94
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:26,430
Give me one month.

95
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:29,070
Why must it be a month? Just go.

96
00:05:29,070 --> 00:05:30,670
I'll only have peace of mind
once you leave.

97
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:32,600
Return to your old self
within a month.

98
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:37,380
Eat well like you always used to,
laugh with Teun Teun,

99
00:05:37,610 --> 00:05:39,740
and complain about
how dead the cafe is.

100
00:05:41,950 --> 00:05:45,150
Once you get back to that,
I'll leave.

101
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:48,450
You and Eun Seol have to be gone
for me to go back to that.

102
00:05:48,450 --> 00:05:49,920
Then try.

103
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:52,020
I'll make an effort too.

104
00:05:52,020 --> 00:05:53,930
What are you going to try?

105
00:05:53,990 --> 00:05:55,430
What do you need
to make an effort for?

106
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:05,440
I'll spend the next month
getting ready to move on.

107
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:09,840
I'll do my best,

108
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:12,140
so please try as well, boss.

109
00:06:14,450 --> 00:06:16,010
That way, I can leave easily.

110
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,860
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

111
00:06:23,860 --> 00:06:25,860
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

112
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:33,130
- Yes?
- The CEO is asking for you.

113
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:37,700
Right, please tell him
I'll be right over to see him.

114
00:07:07,370 --> 00:07:10,370
I think we're in a good place
with the promo video.

115
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:15,040
(Legal Review of PR Materials,
Head of Legal Team Seo Hyun Jae)

116
00:07:18,510 --> 00:07:19,510
What's that?

117
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,880
Are you acting like this
over Team Leader Seo's document?

118
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:25,450
I see you're still grieving.

119
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:28,490
Well, you two were quite fond
of each other.

120
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:31,620
By the way,

121
00:07:31,990 --> 00:07:34,130
wasn't he preparing
for your retrial?

122
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:38,130
What a shame. There's no one left
to help with your retrial.

123
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,770
Maybe you should look
for another lawyer.

124
00:07:40,830 --> 00:07:42,170
I'll help.

125
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:45,870
With your retrial, I mean.

126
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:49,210
Seriously. Who do you think you are?

127
00:07:49,810 --> 00:07:52,010
How can you help
when you're not a lawyer?

128
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,480
What a joke.

129
00:08:08,590 --> 00:08:10,700
Standing beneath a tree,
you don't really feel it.

130
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:16,430
Whether the sun's scorching hot...

131
00:08:19,470 --> 00:08:22,110
or the rain's coming down hard.

132
00:08:23,570 --> 00:08:25,880
Beneath the shelter
that he provided,

133
00:08:29,610 --> 00:08:32,350
I didn't know
how precious that shade was.

134
00:08:33,990 --> 00:08:35,250
I'll never again...

135
00:08:35,590 --> 00:08:38,820
find someone
like the tree he was to me.

136
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,740
(Joo Mi Ran:
Background Investigation Report)

137
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:14,990
Hello, is this Hope Orphanage?

138
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:16,630
Yes, how can I help you?

139
00:09:17,830 --> 00:09:20,430
I'm calling to make an inquiry.

140
00:09:21,330 --> 00:09:23,940
Sure, what do you want to ask?

141
00:09:23,940 --> 00:09:25,900
Did you take in a child...

142
00:09:25,970 --> 00:09:29,170
named Joo Ae Sook
who was born in 1969?

143
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:31,110
May I ask who's calling?

144
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:34,880
Oh, right. I'm...

145
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:38,550
I can't disclose information
about the children at our orphanage.

146
00:09:38,550 --> 00:09:39,880
I'm hanging up now.

147
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:52,960
My dad said
if anything ever happened to him,

148
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:55,470
I need to make sure this gets shown.

149
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:07,810
Hi, Hyun Hee, it's Ko Eun Seol.

150
00:10:08,650 --> 00:10:10,980
Could we meet up for a moment
later this evening?

151
00:10:16,650 --> 00:10:17,690
That's right.

152
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:23,960
My dad used to say it all the time.

153
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:26,430
Back at the orphanage,

154
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:29,300
Ae Sook took care of him
like a mother.

155
00:10:31,370 --> 00:10:33,870
Did he mention anything else?

156
00:10:33,870 --> 00:10:38,140
And he said that same Ae Sook
helped him land a job.

157
00:10:39,010 --> 00:10:41,810
He got hired at Cheongma
through her recommendation.

158
00:10:54,760 --> 00:10:57,700
So, to hide that
she was my birth mother...

159
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:02,230
she planned all of this?

160
00:11:02,730 --> 00:11:06,140
I can't disclose information
about the children at our orphanage.

161
00:11:06,170 --> 00:11:07,710
I'm hanging up now.

162
00:11:12,780 --> 00:11:14,280
I almost forgot.

163
00:11:14,550 --> 00:11:17,550
I scheduled a round of golf
with CEO Park next week.

164
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:18,650
With CEO Park?

165
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:21,220
But he hates golf.

166
00:11:21,220 --> 00:11:24,090
That's only because
his shots weren't going well,

167
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:26,660
but he's been getting
into it lately.

168
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:27,660
Really?

169
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:30,660
Then let Si Hyun's mom and me
come along.

170
00:11:30,730 --> 00:11:32,600
It'll be nice
to get some fresh air together.

171
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,870
Why would you do that?

172
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,700
If we bring the women,
we won't get to play golf at all...

173
00:11:37,770 --> 00:11:39,940
and will just end up
taking photos all day.

174
00:11:40,270 --> 00:11:43,870
Forget it. I'll go with CEO Park,
just the two of us.

175
00:11:45,110 --> 00:11:47,310
Did you work everything out
with him?

176
00:11:47,550 --> 00:11:50,410
Of course.
It's just an overnight trip,

177
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:52,320
so why do we need
our wives' permission?

178
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:54,250
We can just go.

179
00:11:54,250 --> 00:11:56,020
All right, have a good time then.

180
00:11:56,590 --> 00:11:57,690
Okay, good.

181
00:12:21,450 --> 00:12:23,980
Is my wife asleep?

182
00:12:25,550 --> 00:12:26,620
Yes, she is.

183
00:12:35,890 --> 00:12:37,390
Would you like another drink?

184
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:41,830
Sure. Why not?

185
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:50,710
Why don't we...

186
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,080
get some fresh air?

187
00:12:55,050 --> 00:12:57,850
Maybe I've been too tense,
but my head is splitting.

188
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:02,350
I was hoping you'd come with me,
Director Joo.

189
00:13:12,660 --> 00:13:14,870
(Cheongma)

190
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:23,770
Yes, come in.

191
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:28,110
- Have a seat.
- Yes, sir.

192
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:33,880
So Yeon's regular checkup
is coming up soon, right?

193
00:13:34,450 --> 00:13:35,450
Yes, sir.

194
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:39,090
Director Joo will accompany her
this time.

195
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:41,960
That's really not necessary.

196
00:13:42,430 --> 00:13:46,030
From here on out,
So Yeon is practically family to me.

197
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:50,730
I'm just looking out for my family,
so don't feel burdened by it.

198
00:13:53,100 --> 00:13:54,140
Just so you know,

199
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:57,410
I think word has already gotten out.

200
00:13:58,840 --> 00:13:59,840
What do you mean?

201
00:14:00,640 --> 00:14:02,810
You're not getting married
right away,

202
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:04,280
but rumors of your engagement...

203
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:06,950
seem to be circulating
in the stock market.

204
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:09,850
Our shares have been climbing
all morning.

205
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:11,920
Haven't you checked yet?

206
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:16,030
No, I haven't gotten around to that.

207
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,260
In business,

208
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:24,400
you grow by weathering big storms
from time to time.

209
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:28,370
There's a reason they say to strike
while the iron is hot.

210
00:14:29,570 --> 00:14:30,980
This engagement...

211
00:14:31,310 --> 00:14:35,080
is definitely an opportunity
for you, Chief Cha.

212
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:45,920
When will you be done?

213
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,890
Our entire lunch break will be over
at this rate.

214
00:14:48,090 --> 00:14:49,330
I'm pretty much finished.

215
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:55,170
This.

216
00:14:55,230 --> 00:14:56,970
My mom feels uncomfortable
taking it.

217
00:15:00,940 --> 00:15:03,510
What?
So she's refusing to accept it?

218
00:15:03,810 --> 00:15:05,240
It isn't that she doesn't like it,

219
00:15:05,310 --> 00:15:07,240
she just thinks
this sort of thing is unnecessary.

220
00:15:07,610 --> 00:15:09,010
We appreciate the thought, though.

221
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,520
This is what I mean
by her disrespecting me.

222
00:15:13,580 --> 00:15:15,020
Do you know how much effort...

223
00:15:15,090 --> 00:15:16,620
Director Joo and I put
into choosing this?

224
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:18,490
I'm sorry.

225
00:15:18,990 --> 00:15:21,490
Still, we can't just force
a gift on her.

226
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:24,360
She's so difficult.

227
00:15:24,830 --> 00:15:26,430
How many people
must bend over backwards...

228
00:15:26,430 --> 00:15:27,670
just to keep your mother happy?

229
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:30,800
Isn't my dad the one paying
for her regular checkups, too?

230
00:15:31,670 --> 00:15:32,900
Yes, he is.

231
00:15:33,400 --> 00:15:36,610
Everyone is always walking
on eggshells around her.

232
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:39,410
Hae Ra,

233
00:15:40,510 --> 00:15:41,850
please try to understand.

234
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:45,120
That reminds me.

235
00:15:45,650 --> 00:15:48,920
You're all formally invited
to our engagement party.

236
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:50,250
Us, too?

237
00:15:50,490 --> 00:15:51,820
Of course.

238
00:15:52,060 --> 00:15:54,330
Who's going to look out
for my team if not me?

239
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:55,930
Excited, right?

240
00:15:56,190 --> 00:15:57,590
- Yes.
- Yes.

241
00:15:58,200 --> 00:16:00,260
Do you know how expensive
the course meal is?

242
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,270
You won't get to eat like that
anywhere else.

243
00:16:02,900 --> 00:16:05,400
No way. Thank you.

244
00:16:06,140 --> 00:16:08,140
Whatever. Just come empty-handed.

245
00:16:08,370 --> 00:16:10,210
Whatever you bring or give
is going to be pennies anyway.

246
00:16:11,540 --> 00:16:12,540
- Right.
- Sure.

247
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:13,940
Ko Eun Seol.

248
00:16:14,810 --> 00:16:15,980
You be there, too.

249
00:16:16,180 --> 00:16:17,580
Your bosses are getting engaged,

250
00:16:17,650 --> 00:16:19,180
so you should come congratulate us
in person.

251
00:16:19,720 --> 00:16:21,450
Do I really have to go?

252
00:16:21,750 --> 00:16:24,320
Aren't you part of the team?
What now?

253
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:28,090
Do you always have
to act out like this?

254
00:16:28,830 --> 00:16:31,160
Of course not. I'll be there.

255
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:33,400
Sulking around like a total jinx.

256
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:42,870
Eun Seol, have you
pulled yourself together a bit?

257
00:16:43,770 --> 00:16:46,510
Yes, I feel much better now.

258
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:50,380
Losing someone precious to you
so suddenly overnight,

259
00:16:51,050 --> 00:16:53,450
it can't be easy
to process your feelings.

260
00:16:55,250 --> 00:16:58,460
Still, don't rush it,

261
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:01,020
and ease back into your routine
little by little.

262
00:17:01,830 --> 00:17:05,330
You can't stay trapped
in that sense of loss forever.

263
00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:10,870
By the way, Hae Ra is working...

264
00:17:10,930 --> 00:17:14,240
on the scholarship program
these days, right?

265
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:17,410
Yes, she has been
attending the meetings.

266
00:17:18,010 --> 00:17:21,040
I'm sure
she still has a lot to learn.

267
00:17:21,850 --> 00:17:24,950
Well, Director Joo is always
by her side,

268
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:26,450
so that puts my mind at ease.

269
00:17:29,620 --> 00:17:31,620
Chairman Kim.

270
00:17:32,460 --> 00:17:33,460
Yes?

271
00:17:33,790 --> 00:17:35,090
How did Director Joo...

272
00:17:35,090 --> 00:17:38,260
come to work
at the scholarship foundation?

273
00:17:41,170 --> 00:17:44,170
I initially hired her
as Hae Ra's nanny,

274
00:17:44,540 --> 00:17:48,410
but she was so meticulous,
sharp, and capable...

275
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:51,180
that she eventually became
my secretary.

276
00:17:52,010 --> 00:17:53,010
I see.

277
00:17:55,710 --> 00:17:59,180
Did she happen to get married
at any point?

278
00:17:59,180 --> 00:18:01,790
Marriage? Oh, please.

279
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:05,420
She hasn't even dated anyone before.

280
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:08,730
She only ever cares about work,

281
00:18:09,230 --> 00:18:12,730
so she has no interest
in anything else.

282
00:18:12,800 --> 00:18:13,930
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

283
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,870
This punk...

284
00:18:21,070 --> 00:18:23,040
He should be here by now.

285
00:18:28,680 --> 00:18:31,920
Goodness. Mr. Choi, you're here.

286
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:35,020
Behaving yourself today
as well, I see?

287
00:18:35,090 --> 00:18:39,860
Sure am. Once I wrap this up,
I need to go score another big haul.

288
00:18:40,990 --> 00:18:43,530
I admire such diligence.

289
00:18:43,530 --> 00:18:45,830
Mr. Choi, do you have some time?

290
00:18:45,960 --> 00:18:47,800
Since you're here,
why not grab a meal together?

291
00:18:48,170 --> 00:18:52,870
No, thanks. I'm not one
to share a table with just anyone.

292
00:18:55,010 --> 00:18:57,640
That must be because
you grew up pampered.

293
00:18:57,710 --> 00:18:59,280
Well, fine, fair enough.

294
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:01,950
So what's on your schedule
for the rest of the day?

295
00:19:01,950 --> 00:19:05,280
Wrap this up, score big,

296
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:07,850
and have dinner
with the motel owner.

297
00:19:07,890 --> 00:19:10,420
I see. Sounds good.

298
00:19:10,850 --> 00:19:13,860
Hit it big
and bring in a huge score.

299
00:19:14,830 --> 00:19:15,830
See you.

300
00:19:15,930 --> 00:19:17,790
Sure, take care.

301
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:27,700
That kid is disgustingly diligent.

302
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:30,140
How does he never miss a day
and always show up?

303
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:35,250
My Ae Sook...

304
00:19:36,110 --> 00:19:38,450
used to be known
for her diligence too.

305
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:43,620
What happened?

306
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:50,560
Unbelievable. Let's go.

307
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:52,430
Darn. What do I do?

308
00:19:56,170 --> 00:19:59,640
No matter how much I think about it,
they look alike.

309
00:20:03,270 --> 00:20:04,610
What bugs me,

310
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:08,880
I have to check
with my own two eyes.

311
00:20:18,360 --> 00:20:21,020
You're going on a trip
with a friend?

312
00:20:21,690 --> 00:20:25,130
Yes. With the hometown friend
I mentioned before.

313
00:20:25,830 --> 00:20:28,700
You've been seeing that friend
a lot lately.

314
00:20:30,370 --> 00:20:32,940
Maybe because we reconnected late,
it feels more special.

315
00:20:33,200 --> 00:20:35,670
- Precious, too.
- Really?

316
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:41,280
You'll probably take lots of photos
on your trip.

317
00:20:41,680 --> 00:20:44,950
The weather is nice these days,
so they'll turn out great.

318
00:20:47,250 --> 00:20:50,150
I'm curious about this friend too.

319
00:20:52,590 --> 00:20:55,460
Show me some photos
when you get back.

320
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:58,760
- Photos?
- Yes.

321
00:21:00,400 --> 00:21:02,600
Anyway, eat plenty
of delicious food,

322
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:05,670
and have a wonderful time,
Director Joo.

323
00:21:07,270 --> 00:21:08,270
Sure.

324
00:21:42,210 --> 00:21:45,910
(Jun Hwan: Off work at 6 p.m.)

325
00:21:49,810 --> 00:21:51,580
- I'm home.
- You're back?

326
00:21:51,980 --> 00:21:54,180
- Where's Grandma?
- She went to the senior center.

327
00:21:54,450 --> 00:21:56,550
Hey, Eun Guk.
Come sit down for a minute.

328
00:22:03,230 --> 00:22:04,490
Listen,

329
00:22:05,330 --> 00:22:07,660
did anything happen
between you and Teun Teun's mom?

330
00:22:09,130 --> 00:22:12,370
- Why do you ask?
- Well, she asked us...

331
00:22:12,670 --> 00:22:14,440
to move out of the house.

332
00:22:14,870 --> 00:22:17,810
She even handed us cash
and told us to leave.

333
00:22:17,910 --> 00:22:19,210
When I asked
if it was because of you,

334
00:22:19,280 --> 00:22:20,510
she couldn't even answer.

335
00:22:21,040 --> 00:22:23,310
Technically speaking,
it's not because of me.

336
00:22:23,850 --> 00:22:24,920
What do you mean?

337
00:22:24,980 --> 00:22:27,480
If not you,
then who else could it be?

338
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:30,450
The truth is,
I think Attorney Seo died...

339
00:22:30,890 --> 00:22:32,860
while trying to help Eun Seol.

340
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:35,730
What? While helping Eun Seol?

341
00:22:37,590 --> 00:22:39,430
His death seems to be tied
to Eun Seol's retrial...

342
00:22:39,500 --> 00:22:40,960
that he was preparing.

343
00:22:42,330 --> 00:22:43,800
The boss was asked...

344
00:22:43,870 --> 00:22:45,900
if any of the attorney's belongings
could be evidence,

345
00:22:46,500 --> 00:22:47,900
which is how she found out.

346
00:22:53,980 --> 00:22:55,250
I see.

347
00:22:57,610 --> 00:22:58,720
From what I heard,

348
00:22:58,980 --> 00:23:01,320
it seems Attorney Seo
liked Eun Seol a lot.

349
00:23:02,850 --> 00:23:04,760
Eun Seol appreciated him,

350
00:23:04,990 --> 00:23:07,190
but she never thought of him
in a romantic way.

351
00:23:08,730 --> 00:23:10,460
Wait, if Teun Teun's mom...

352
00:23:11,060 --> 00:23:12,960
found that out,

353
00:23:13,430 --> 00:23:16,000
she must have a lot of hard feelings
toward Eun Seol.

354
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:18,200
Yes.

355
00:23:19,270 --> 00:23:20,670
Then what are you going to do?

356
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:23,610
Can you let go of your feelings
for Teun Teun's mom?

357
00:23:25,080 --> 00:23:26,110
No.

358
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:28,250
I'll never leave her.

359
00:23:29,650 --> 00:23:31,550
I really like her, Dad.

360
00:23:32,580 --> 00:23:33,580
Actually,

361
00:23:34,050 --> 00:23:35,090
I love her.

362
00:23:42,460 --> 00:23:44,360
(Joo Ae Sook's Baby (F)
Sept. 11, 2000, 11:05 p.m., 3.28kg)

363
00:23:48,730 --> 00:23:52,070
Did she happen to get married
at any point?

364
00:23:52,370 --> 00:23:54,770
Marriage? Oh, please.

365
00:23:54,970 --> 00:23:58,510
She hasn't even dated anyone before.

366
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:05,450
So she hid having me?

367
00:24:06,320 --> 00:24:08,520
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

368
00:24:08,590 --> 00:24:09,590
Come in.

369
00:24:16,360 --> 00:24:19,630
Gosh, what brings you here
at this hour, Eun Seol?

370
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:23,870
Ms. Joo, if you have time,

371
00:24:24,330 --> 00:24:25,940
would you like
to have dinner together?

372
00:24:27,500 --> 00:24:29,510
Sure, I would love to.

373
00:24:32,180 --> 00:24:34,410
You've been seeking me out
quite a bit lately.

374
00:24:35,110 --> 00:24:38,010
Why did you want to see me today?

375
00:24:39,780 --> 00:24:42,920
I was just curious about you.

376
00:24:44,150 --> 00:24:45,520
You're curious about me?

377
00:24:46,060 --> 00:24:47,060
Yes.

378
00:24:48,190 --> 00:24:49,190
My mom...

379
00:24:55,830 --> 00:24:58,770
You were friends with my mom.

380
00:25:00,440 --> 00:25:02,770
I was curious about your life story.

381
00:25:05,810 --> 00:25:07,110
My life story?

382
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:10,180
You mean, like my past?

383
00:25:11,310 --> 00:25:12,320
Yes.

384
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:16,050
Well, you know everything
about mine.

385
00:25:16,090 --> 00:25:17,320
That's true.

386
00:25:17,620 --> 00:25:19,860
How could I not know about yours?

387
00:25:20,860 --> 00:25:22,390
So I was wondering.

388
00:25:23,660 --> 00:25:24,790
Do you also...

389
00:25:25,900 --> 00:25:28,930
have a past you wish
you could erase, just like me?

390
00:25:31,670 --> 00:25:32,740
Well...

391
00:25:33,400 --> 00:25:35,610
I never dwell on the past.

392
00:25:36,470 --> 00:25:38,140
There's no point
in being bound by it.

393
00:25:38,210 --> 00:25:39,880
It just gets in the way.

394
00:25:43,880 --> 00:25:46,680
I don't really have a past
worth mentioning.

395
00:25:47,080 --> 00:25:49,520
I've just worked nonstop
since graduation.

396
00:25:49,990 --> 00:25:52,360
In a way, it has been an easy life.

397
00:25:58,830 --> 00:25:59,960
By any chance,

398
00:26:02,230 --> 00:26:04,670
is there anything
you want to know about me?

399
00:26:06,970 --> 00:26:08,640
About you, Eun Seol?

400
00:26:17,610 --> 00:26:18,620
Not really.

401
00:26:36,730 --> 00:26:38,900
I never dwell on the past.

402
00:26:39,740 --> 00:26:41,370
There's no point
in being bound by it.

403
00:26:41,470 --> 00:26:42,940
It just gets in the way.

404
00:26:45,110 --> 00:26:46,110
Did you...

405
00:26:48,780 --> 00:26:51,480
only see me
as a weight around your neck?

406
00:27:00,720 --> 00:27:01,730
Where are you going?

407
00:27:02,090 --> 00:27:03,160
To my part-time shift
at the restaurant.

408
00:27:03,460 --> 00:27:05,260
Dae Sik opened a barbecue place.

409
00:27:06,630 --> 00:27:09,330
How long are you going to keep
filling in at restaurants?

410
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:12,540
Even if it's tiny,
you should open a place of your own.

411
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:15,810
I'm heading out.
Don't forget to grab lunch.

412
00:27:18,540 --> 00:27:21,710
When will we ever buy a house
saving pennies like this?

413
00:27:23,810 --> 00:27:24,810
Wait, no.

414
00:27:25,850 --> 00:27:27,680
Many drops make a shower, right?

415
00:27:32,790 --> 00:27:35,960
Right then,
let's make a killing playing cards.

416
00:27:36,690 --> 00:27:39,360
With those winnings,
we can finally move!

417
00:27:45,340 --> 00:27:46,800
What did you say
you were doing this weekend?

418
00:27:47,340 --> 00:27:49,270
I'm going to a show with my mom.

419
00:27:50,210 --> 00:27:51,370
Want me to join you?

420
00:27:53,110 --> 00:27:54,180
Maybe next time.

421
00:27:54,740 --> 00:27:57,110
My mom just wants
the two of us to go this time.

422
00:27:57,180 --> 00:27:58,520
Are you kidding me?

423
00:27:58,720 --> 00:28:01,050
It feels like I'm competing
with your mom over you.

424
00:28:01,420 --> 00:28:03,620
What is this, a love triangle?

425
00:28:03,690 --> 00:28:05,760
Instead, we're together all week.

426
00:28:05,760 --> 00:28:07,790
We even have lunch together
like this every day.

427
00:28:08,430 --> 00:28:09,790
Whatever.

428
00:28:10,030 --> 00:28:12,430
It's as if your mom
steals you from me every weekend.

429
00:28:13,260 --> 00:28:14,260
Just let it slide this week.

430
00:28:15,270 --> 00:28:17,430
Come on, I'll buy you a nice lunch.

431
00:28:18,840 --> 00:28:20,140
You didn't even
book a table anywhere.

432
00:28:30,050 --> 00:28:31,050
Can we help you with something?

433
00:28:31,280 --> 00:28:32,280
What is this?

434
00:28:32,320 --> 00:28:33,520
You see,

435
00:28:33,980 --> 00:28:36,250
I made a mistake
with the lady here last time.

436
00:28:37,590 --> 00:28:38,590
You remember me, right?

437
00:28:40,390 --> 00:28:41,390
Yes, I remember.

438
00:28:42,230 --> 00:28:43,230
What about it?

439
00:28:43,490 --> 00:28:46,900
I said I'd pay for dry cleaning,
but I never got around to it.

440
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:49,030
It kept weighing on my conscience.

441
00:28:49,500 --> 00:28:50,500
Forget it.

442
00:28:51,170 --> 00:28:52,770
Are you serious? How pathetic.

443
00:28:54,670 --> 00:28:58,340
If you give me your business card,
I'll wire you the money later.

444
00:28:58,370 --> 00:28:59,540
I said, forget it.

445
00:28:59,540 --> 00:29:02,280
Why would I trust a man like you
and give you my business card?

446
00:29:02,350 --> 00:29:03,510
Are you kidding me?

447
00:29:05,950 --> 00:29:07,180
It's all right.

448
00:29:07,180 --> 00:29:08,750
You really don't need
to compensate her.

449
00:29:09,020 --> 00:29:12,490
No, I insist.
I must pay for the dry cleaning.

450
00:29:12,560 --> 00:29:13,920
It's the right thing to do.

451
00:29:16,090 --> 00:29:17,190
Then...

452
00:29:18,630 --> 00:29:19,730
Here's my card.

453
00:29:19,930 --> 00:29:21,530
(Cha Seok Jin)

454
00:29:22,970 --> 00:29:25,030
Why are you giving your card
to this stranger?

455
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:26,440
Can't you tell
just by looking at him?

456
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:28,200
He's a con artist.

457
00:29:29,170 --> 00:29:30,570
Get off me!

458
00:29:30,770 --> 00:29:32,980
- What do you think you're doing?
- Darn it.

459
00:30:04,610 --> 00:30:08,610
(A Trap Called Desire)

460
00:30:08,680 --> 00:30:10,980
So I guess
I'll be alone this weekend.

461
00:30:11,050 --> 00:30:13,250
Where do you stand on Director Joo?

462
00:30:13,250 --> 00:30:16,520
Who's taking Team Leader Seo's death
the hardest right now?

463
00:30:16,590 --> 00:30:18,890
If Ko Eun Seol digs into
Team Leader Seo's case,

464
00:30:18,960 --> 00:30:20,460
who'll be in the most danger?

465
00:30:20,460 --> 00:30:23,960
This time, we'll see to it
that Attorney Seo gets justice.

466
00:30:24,460 --> 00:30:27,530
From time to time,
she seems to recall false memories.

467
00:30:27,600 --> 00:30:30,030
I just wish she stays quiet
at my engagement party.

468
00:30:30,100 --> 00:30:32,670
Do you have something to say to me?
You have that look in your eyes.

469
00:30:32,770 --> 00:30:34,040
Now that it's come to this,

470
00:30:34,100 --> 00:30:36,240
let's just say
I gave birth to Ko Eun Seol.

471
00:30:36,570 --> 00:30:39,780
If I claim I'm her birth mother,
what can she really do?

472
00:30:40,910 --> 00:30:42,910
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
